"""A surface detector for definite articles, principally English 'the'.

Lowercase ' the' is strongest after prepositions and weakest after 'all',
copulas and opening quotes. Capitalized forms respond mainly at sentence or
line beginnings; an attached 'the' fragment instead has a negative response.
For other preceding words, verbs strengthen the response and nouns or
numbers weaken it. Smaller responses cover other European definite articles.
Document starts have a negative response; initial 'Title:' has a large spike.
Only the current token, the preceding token and document position are used.
