Short fin/fun syllables and the unusual clusters fn, fm, fp, fw and fx
are negative; short fil/ful/fit/fut syllables are positive. The same
patterns can straddle a token boundary. Many frequent complete English words
are suppressed. Function abbreviations are strengthened after newlines,
indentation, or the Rust keyword pub. These are approximate spelling rules, not
a general phonetic analysis of words containing f. The training examples
point to these local spellings rather than to a shared topic or meaning.
